From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:04:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aot: host overrides of SDK functions, thread exit, runs
 without a memory snapshot, cache maintenance, fault registers

ModuleSet.build(overrides=...) replaces exported functions by host functions (the Mach host's HLE_FORCE): not lifted, their stub reaches the function registered at the address. Aot.run takes snapshot=False (a game's heap is gigabytes) and returns x29/x30/sp on a fault. aot_request_exit ends a guest thread from its svc handler without unwinding through Python. SYS (DC, IC) lifts as an asynchronous hyper call that sets none: the runtime falls through. Tests: overrides, DC/IC, FADDP (found by Xenoblade 2's sdk).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: S7bis Linux Horizon layer and AOT support found booting Xenoblade Chronicles 2; tests use synthetic code and fake guest memory, no game data
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch swann/jalon-s7bis-xc2)

